# Trivy ignore list — reviewed, non-applicable advisories only.
# An advisory accepted in osv-scanner.toml is mirrored here, and in
# pnpm.auditConfig.ignoreGhsas (package.json), only where Trivy or pnpm audit
# would otherwise report it. Keep the rationale in sync wherever an entry
# appears. The lists differ on purpose, as of 2026-11-08:
#   - deepmerge GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4 is in osv-scanner.toml only. GitHub rates
#     it Low, below this scan's CRITICAL/HIGH and below both levels the repo
#     runs pnpm audit at (high in security.yml, moderate in guard:audit-clean).
#   - minimatch GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 was in osv-scanner.toml and
#     pnpm.auditConfig only, never here (Moderate, below this scan's
#     CRITICAL/HIGH). Both entries were removed on 2026-11-08: GitHub
#     corrected the advisory's range to start at 7.0.0, so minimatch 3.1.5 is
#     out of it and the entries were unused.
#   - brace-expansion GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg is here only. osv-scanner.toml
#     dropped it once the overrides cleared it, and its pnpm.auditConfig mirror
#     was removed on 2026-11-08: pnpm audit reported nothing without it
#     (checked 2026-10-30 and 2026-11-08). The two entries below are dead too
#     (Trivy 0.69.3 with the 2026-11-08 DB reports nothing for brace-expansion
#     without them) and left for their own removal. Until then they would hide
#     a regression below the override pins from Trivy (the OSV gates and pnpm
#     audit would catch it), and the comment below names versions the lockfile
#     no longer has.
#   - image-size GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq and GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr were in all three
#     lists until metro 0.83.8 took image-size out of the lockfile; the three
#     copies were removed together.
# Every entry below is against pnpm-lock.yaml. This file is also the only one
# of the three that covers apps/blackout-server/poetry.lock (the OSV gates and
# pnpm audit read pnpm-lock.yaml alone); the four Twisted 26.4.0 entries it
# held for that lock left with the change that locked Twisted 26.10.0.
# Records: docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-30.md,
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-10-31.md,
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-2026-11-08.md,
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-image-size-2026-11-02.md and
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-twisted-2026-11-02.md.

# brace-expansion ReDoS. The tree resolves to 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.8, all at or
# above the maintainer's per-line security patches (1.1.12/2.0.2/5.0.8); OSV's
# affected-versions list for the 1.x line tops out at 1.1.11, so 1.1.16 is
# patched. The scanners over-report across major lines. CVE-2026-14257 is the
# CVE alias of GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (Trivy matches by CVE); both are listed.
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg
CVE-2026-14257
